    {
      "version": "0.2.0",
      "tag": "v0.2.0",
      "date": "2026-09-26",
      "notes": "- **macOS and Linux builds, at last.** Releases are now built automatically by\n  GitHub Actions for Windows, Linux, and macOS (both Apple Silicon and Intel)\n  every time a version tag is pushed, instead of only what could be built on\n  a Windows machine by hand.\n- **Cloud backup**: manually back up and restore a profile snapshot from\n  Settings → Backup (gated behind the same plan as the AI tutor).\n- **General notes importer** replaces the Obsidian-specific one, with\n  broader compatibility.\n- Fixed a bug where closing one database connection could silently close\n  every other open profile's connection too, breaking Import with\n  \"attempted to acquire a connection on a closed pool\".\n- Fixed the sidebar version badge overflowing its box.\n- Entitlement verification now uses the real signing key end-to-end.",
